It looks like your terminal is completely back to normal and working fine now.
However, your prompt still shows ajay@Inspiron:~/Desktop/GitStartup/git-journey$, which means the Git branch name is still hidden.
Let's turn it on right now using the easiest, safest method that does not require editing any files manually.
## Step 1: Run these commands
Copy and paste these three commands into your terminal one by one and press Enter:

echo "source /usr/lib/git-core/git-sh-prompt" >> ~/.bashrc

echo "export PS1='\[\e[32m\]\u@\h\[\e[m\]:\[\e[34m\]\w\[\e[m\]\[\e[33m\]\$(__git_ps1 \" (%s)\")\[\e[m\]\$ '" >> ~/.bashrc

source ~/.bashrc

## Step 2: Look at your prompt
As soon as you run that last source command, your terminal prompt will instantly change to look exactly like this:
ajay@Inspiron:~/Desktop/GitStartup/git-journey (main)$
